  "answer": "All three modules are updated. Here's a summary of the changes:\n\n## `defaults.mjs`\n- `DEFAULT_OPTIONS` now exposes all three defaults: `{ precision: 2, prefix: '', unitLabel: '' }`. It is a plain frozen-in-spirit constant that is never mutated.\n\n## `resolver.mjs`\n- `resolveOptions(overrides = {})` now:\n  - Treats `undefined` as no overrides.\n  - Throws `TypeError` for `null`, non-objects, and arrays.\n  - Throws `TypeError` for unknown keys.\n  - Validates `precision` as an integer 0–4 (`RangeError` otherwise).\n  - Validates `prefix` and `unitLabel` as strings (`TypeError` otherwise).\n  - Returns a **fresh** object built from `DEFAULT_OPTIONS` values, so callers never share mutable state with the defaults or with each other.\n- Only own fields are considered (via `hasOwnProperty`), so inherited properties are ignored.\n\n## `formatter.mjs`\n- `formatValue(value, overrides = {})` now:\n  - Throws `TypeError` for non-finite / non-number values.\n  - Delegates option resolution to `resolveOptions`.\n  - Appends `\" \" + unitLabel` only when `unitLabel` is nonempty.\n  - Preserves old call forms (`formatValue(12.345)` → `\"12.35\"`, `{ precision: 1, prefix: '~' }` → `\"~12.3\"`).\n\nThe existing exports `DEFAULT_OPTIONS`, `resolveOptions`, and `formatValue` are all preserved, and the provided `public.test.mjs` expectations (`\"12.35\"`, `\"~12.3\"`, `\"12.30 kg\"`, and the resolver output) are satisfied.",
